{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Final rebar-debug report (pre-Gerrit).\n\nProblem: the locked N=3000 importer integration test consumed 77-90s locally while preserving 3,000 creates, 3,000 comments and 24 import commits.\n\nProven root cause: the bulk path performed 6,000 subprocess-backed user.name lookups and 3,000 whole-staging-root stale sweeps. Full cProfile attributed 47.790s to 6,001 _git_config calls and 15.938s to the sweeps; controlled identical-state A/B removed 60.827s (78.8%) by replacing only those collaborators.\n\nTest/proof: tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py was strengthened as the physically held-out RED oracle. Before the fix its unchanged state/commit assertions passed and collaborator counts failed (6000, 3000) vs (1, 12). After the held-out fix it passed at 17.76-19.14s. Independent defect mutations returned RED: no author scope => (6000, 12), 72.34s; per-item sweep => (1, 3000), 33.51s. A copied-context isolation oracle then exposed mutable ContextVar sharing (copied miss leaked copied-1 into the parent); copy-on-write made it GREEN, and restoring mutation returned RED.\n\nFix: explicit import-scoped, fallback-keyed, copy-on-write author caching plus at most one stale-staging sweep for the first new ticket in each bounded batch. Direct/interactive callers retain live lookup and sweep defaults. No dependency, external effect, durability rule, event content, commit-count rule, or coverage was removed.\n\nReplication: same-host N=3000 reproduction completed in 17.040s with 3,000 CREATE + 3,000 COMMENT files, exactly 24 commits, one user.name read, 12 stale sweeps, clean index, and an idempotent zero-write rerun. Compared with counted baseline 77.231s, wall time fell 60.191s (77.9%); author reads fell 6,000x and sweeps 250x.\n\nSafety: 52 focused import/store tests passed in 67.56s; lint, format, complexity, actionlint/zizmor, and mypy passed. Full default selection under xdist: 12,841 passed, 52 skipped; sole failure is pre-existing origin/main src/rebar/_config_schema.py at 808 LOC against the 800 cap, unrelated to this diff and already covered by cinderlike-lucky-akitainu. No test was weakened.\n\nCaller/sibling sweep: single writes, reconciler stage_event callers, claim/close/delete and ordinary event writes retain defaults/live behavior; no additional production sibling needed a change. CLI/library/import surfaces converge on the same importer/core, so no parity gap. Residual risk: repo-wide size headroom remains tracked on cinderlike-lucky-akitainu; accepted as outside this latency change."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786641866090814001,"uuid":"34c8d322-2cc0-44af-a7a8-6b26f30ba1d0"}